/*
  alright now that we have the knowlage to save into flash we need to know how to read and use the date from
  flash in memory cuz thats were our code will run and for that Arduino Core again has some functions or macro?
  i dont know what they are called tbh but its a function but is written as a macro with \ to write a new a line
  BUT thats not important just ask ai or something but to read/use we use pgm_read_byte, pgm_read_word, pgm_read_dword and
  pgm_read_qword. when do you use what you may ask? well its pretty simpel byte if your reg you need is 8bit word if your
  register is 16bit and so on. thats btw not some random ahhh thing but actualy how we describe 16 bit just like we 
  describe 8bit as a byte an dword just stands for double word and qword for quad word crazy ik.

  here is digitalWrite as an example:
*/
void digitalWrite(uint8_t pin, bool val)
{
    // this look more complicated than it is looks we just make pointer that points to a register
    // and because a register isnt just accesably trough memory we need a volatule uintbit_t * and pass the
    // register through reference
    volatile uint8_t* port_p { reinterpret_cast<volatile uint8_t*>(pgm_read_byte(&pin_table[pin].port)) };
    uint8_t mask {pgm_read_byte(pin_table[pin].mask)};

    if (val) { // the rest is just like we know it thats it
        *port_p |= mask;
    } else {
        *port_p &=~ mask;
    } 
}
